config: small memos and trims in the per-package config work

Sub-series: K (config trims) - patch 1 of 1; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: unchanged (line numbers only)

Smaller savings in the per-package config work: getUseMask() and
getUseForce() reuse the stacked result for equal token lists, the
ACCEPT_LICENSE stack of getMissingLicenses() is remembered per token
tuple (not when "*" makes it depend on the package), config._getitem()
finds a missing key without raising KeyError once per dict, and setcpv()
builds the RESTRICT/PROPERTIES USE set once instead of twice.

This is the config part of patch 0025 of the 25-patch ladder
(config-trims-and-leftovers), which is now patches 0022, 0025, 0026, 0027
and 0030. As a step of the second order that was measured (chain-prelim2)
these config trims were 4.5 s; the pieces of 0025 were not measured one by
one in the final order. Together, on top of patches 0001-0024: sum of six
states 95.9 -> 90.5 s (-5.5 s, -1.2 % of the stock sum 447.5). Alone on
stock 3.0.83: see README (sub-series K).

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21; cut out of its
former patch on 2026-11-21 without changing a line of code. Not a
human-written change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on
six states of one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the
same merge list in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts
and the same package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
